Following other projects' behaviour
-----------------------------------
These files are the Tango authors' code; they follow documented or observed behaviour of other projects, which they
cite:
  - tools/template_model.py, tools/template_golden.py: the model of the picture above (Template_MiSTer's behaviour).
  - tools/vproc_golden.py, tools/vproc_audio.py, tools/vproc_board.py, sim/measure_scale.py: models of MiSTer's video
    and audio processing (Template_MiSTer sys/: ascal, video_freak.sv, audio_out.sv, iir_filter.v), with the
    framework's models in sys/build_tools/ (sys-tango; their own licences).
  - sim/tb_template.cpp, sim/tb_template.inc, sim/tb_vproc.v: the BL616 side of the link as the FPGA Companion firmware
    (Apache-2.0) and the Tango firmware (firmware-tango, GPL-3.0-or-later) drive it.
  - The menu string format (CONF_STR) and the core interface are MiSTer's (sys-tango's NOTICE).
  - sim/run_vproc_gates.sh and tools/vproc_audio.py load MiSTer's filter files (Filters, Gamma, Shadow_Masks, Presets,
    Filters_Audio) from a folder the user gives (FILTERS); none is in this repository.


